NAME
    xxd, hexdump - hexdump a real file's raw bytes

SYNOPSIS
    xxd <path>
    hexdump <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Reads <path>'s REAL bytes off disk (not decoded as text the way
    'cat'/'head'/'tail' do, which would corrupt anything that isn't valid
    UTF8) and prints them in the same address/hex/ASCII layout 'mem' uses
    for a live memory space - the on-disk counterpart to 'mem', purpose-
    built so a 'dump'd capture can be inspected without leaving the shell
    for an external hex editor. Walled to the project's own directory tree
    (see 'cd'). With no <path>, hexdumps piped stdin instead - UTF8-encoded
    first, since a pipeline stage's own output is always already-decoded
    text here, never raw bytes (this shell's pipes have no byte-stream
    concept the way a real Unix pipe does). 'hexdump' is a plain alias, not
    a separate command - and NOT real hexdump's own multi-format output,
    just this same one layout under a second, equally-reached-for name.

EXAMPLES
    dump WRAM 0 256 wram.bin
    xxd home/Logs/SNES/wram.bin
    echo hi | xxd
